# Zod schema first for data contracts

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L1 contracts.

## Use This When

- Data enters from outside the trusted core: user input, command parameters, environment variables, network messages, files, generated test data.

## Stop Here If

- The data has one Zod schema and its static type is `z.infer` of that schema.

## Core rule

- Data contracts are Zod schemas; behavioural contracts (ports) are TypeScript interfaces.
- Import Zod from `@workspace/zod`, the single instance with the shared error map.
- Validate once at the boundary, trust inside. `unknown` comes in, `parse` turns it into a typed value; `any` is not allowed (`no-any.mdc`).
- Identifiers are validated with the entity-id schemas from the `@workspace/ids` registry.
- Command parameter schemas are generated by `bun run model` from the `.surql` headers; do not hand-write a parallel schema.
